Description: include=FILE reads servers and secrets from a root-only file
 pam_tacplus takes its shared secret only as a module argument, which puts
 it in world-readable /etc/pam.d. include=FILE adds the server=, secret= and
 timeout= lines of FILE to the arguments, as the Cumulus and VyOS forks do;
 NuDanOS keeps the file root-only (0600). A make check test covers it.
Author: NuDanOS Maintainers <jon@fernandez.tech>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-06
